#+begin_export latex
Define the data-dependent parameter $\theta(P, \text{Data}_a)$ as
\begin{equation*}
  \theta(P; \text{Data}_a) = \text{BLP}_P[s_0(Z) \mid S(Z; \text{Data}_a)].
\end{equation*}
The data-dependent ``median'' parameter $\theta_{\text{M}}(P,
\text{Data})$ is defined as
\begin{equation*}
  \theta_{\text{M}}(P, \text{Data}) = \text{Median}_{A \sim U(\mathcal{A})}(\theta(P; \text{Data}_A) \mid \text{Data}).
\end{equation*}

\vfill

Would the parameter \( \theta(P; \text{Data}) \) be more
interesting, i.e., easier to interpret?

\vfill

Would we expect the parameter \( \theta_{\text{M}}(P; \text{Data}_a) \) to
be close to \( \theta(P; \text{Data}) \)?
#+end_export


